    "id": "finding_2_dissociation",
    "statement": "Deformity and densitometric status dissociate, and the dissociation carries prognostic weight: a stratum of patients graded at or above the moderate deformity floor is densitometrically normal or osteopenic, and that stratum carries a higher five-year incidence of major osteoporotic fracture than densitometrically normal patients without deformity.",
